# URL routing for the site. Cloudflare applies these on deploy; web/vite.config.js
# parses this same file for `npm run dev` / `vite preview`, so the two cannot drift.
#
# 1. Pretty, shareable URLs for the reader's markdown shell:
#
#      /wiki/en-US/cell-death/Eryptosis
#      /tasks/en-US/task_output_parthanatos_open_questions_08_Sep_2026
#
#    rewrite (200, not 301) to pages/md-viewer.html, which fetches the note and
#    sets rel=canonical back to the pretty path above — so the URL a user saves,
#    bookmarks, or iframes is this one, and the ?src= form stays an
#    implementation detail of the reader iframe.
#
#    NOTE on the `?kind=&src=` in the targets: a 200 rewrite is server-internal,
#    so the browser URL stays `/wiki/…` and that query NEVER reaches the shell's
#    location.search. md-viewer therefore derives the note from
#    location.pathname (see noteFromPathname), not from the target query — the
#    pathname is the only channel. The query is kept anyway: it documents the
#    mapping, and the ?src= form must keep working for the reader iframe.
#
# 2. The `*.md` identity rules MUST stay above the `/*` splats. md-viewer fetches
#    each note by its real path (`../wiki/en-US/_link/Urolithin A.md`); a bare
#    `/wiki/*` splat would swallow that fetch and return HTML, and every note
#    would fail to render. These map the request to itself so the static asset
#    wins. First match wins in Cloudflare _redirects, so the order is load-bearing.
#
# Targets keep the `.html` extension: under the default html_handling an
# extension-less target triggers Cloudflare's own 307 and the query string is
# lost with it.

/wiki/*.md    /wiki/:splat.md    200
/tasks/*.md   /tasks/:splat.md   200
/wiki/*    /pages/md-viewer.html?kind=wiki&src=wiki/:splat.md   200
/tasks/*   /pages/md-viewer.html?kind=task&src=tasks/:splat.md  200
